{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I sell the morning paper, sir My name is Jimmy [D]Brown,
[D]Everybody knows I am The Newsboy of the [G]town.
[G]You will hear me yelling "Morning Star", As I run along the [D]street,
[D]I have no hat upon my head, No shoes upon my [G]feet.
[Em]I have no hat upon my head, No shoes [C]upon my [G]feet
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I'm awful cold and hungry, sir, My clothes are worn and thin,
I wander 'bout from place to place, My daily bread to win.
Never mind, sir, how I look, Don't look at me and frown,
I sell the morning papers, sir, My name is Jimmy Brown.
I sell the morning papers, sir, My name is Jimmy Brown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
My Father died a drunkard, sir, I've heard my Mother say,
And I am helping Mother, sir, As I journey on my way.
Mother always tells me, sir, I've nothing in this world to lose,
I'll get a place in Heaven, sir, To sell the Gospel News.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Never mind sir how I look, Don't look at me and frown,
I sell the morning papers, sir, My name is Jimmy Brown.
I sell the morning papers, sir, My name is Jimmy Brown.
{end_of_verse}
